sorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"G000583","fullName":"Rep. Gottheimer, Josh [D-NJ-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"G000600","fullName":"Rep. Perez, Marie Gluesenkamp [D-WA-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WA"},{"bioguideId":"C001055","fullName":"Rep. Case, Ed [D-HI-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"HI"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T13:59:29+00:00","id":"hr438-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-15","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-20","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Health."},"laws":[],"number":"438","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"L000598","district":1,"fullName":"Rep. LaLota, Nick [R-NY-1]","party":"R","state":"NY"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-15","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><b>PFC Joseph P. Dwyer Peer Support Program Act</b></p> <p>This bill requires the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) to establish the PFC Joseph P. Dwyer Peer Support Program to make grants to eligible entities for peer-to-peer mental health programs for veterans. </p> <p>Eligible entities include (1) a nonprofit organization that has historically served the mental health needs of veterans; (2) a congressionally chartered veteran service organization; or (3) a state, local, or tribal veteran service agency, director, or commissioner. </p> <p>The VA shall establish an advisory committee to create appropriate program standards.</p>","updateDate":"2025-02-14T21:54:38Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"PFC Joseph P. Dwyer Peer Support Program Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:07:40Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:07:40Z"}
